# WC3 UI Designer — Core

Electron/TypeScript tool for designing Warcraft III Reforged UI frames and exporting JASS, Lua, or TypeScript for maps.

## Entry points

- `src/ts/app.ts` → `src/ts/main.ts` (main process)
- `src/ts/renderer.ts` (renderer bootstrap)

## Core model

- `ProjectTree`, `FrameComponent`, `CustomComplex`, `FrameBuilder` — frame state
- `Commands/Implementation/` — undoable mutations
- `Export.ts`, `Templates.ts`, `FrameMLText.ts` — generated map code

## Rules

- Keep changes minimal; match existing class layout. Remove dead code during reworks.
- Do not edit build outputs in `app/`, `Build/`, or `dist/` unless explicitly requested.
- Route undoable frame mutations through command classes, not direct frame setters.
- Preserve save-file compatibility; load new persisted fields defensively.

## Verification

- `npm run compile-ts` after TypeScript changes
- `npm run lint` for broad or style-sensitive edits
- `npm run start` requires `src/ts/configMain.ts` (see README.md)

## Skills

- General editor work → `.cursor/skills/wc3-ui-designer`
- Undo/redo commands → `.cursor/skills/wc3-undo-commands`
- Export templates / generated WC3 code → `.cursor/skills/wc3-export-safety`
